    "created_at": "2025-09-11T17:24:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-11T17:24:56Z",
    "body": "If I understand the spec correctly, the one use case this doesn't solve well is an exit animation. Using this will delay sending the request for the next page, so a 250ms animation could add up to 250ms of additional latency which isn't ideal.  It would be useful to have a way to delay freezing and unloading the page without delaying the next page, especially for cross-doc VTs like I described above. ",
